WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:05.259
We've come up with our own viewing order for
the DCEU that we believe does the best job

00:00:05.259 --> 00:00:09.250
of introducing you to the characters, building
the universe, and getting you hyped for what

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.280
happens next.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.960
So take a look at the right order to watch
every DC Extended Universe movie.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.840
Wonder Woman takes place during World War
I, which means that chronologically, it's

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.800
the first film in the DCEU by a good margin.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.160
That's not the main reason why we've selected
it for our number one spot, though.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:29.720
Wonder Woman is also the best-reviewed film
in DC's lineup, and when you're beginning

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:34.120
a lengthy movie marathon like this, it definitely
helps to start off on the right foot.

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:38.010
Kicking off with what's arguably the best
movie in the series will definitely give you

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:40.840
some motivation to keep watching if things
get a little rough.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:46.820
"I am… above average."

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:51.590
The film also does a great job of introducing
Wonder Woman as a character, which will give

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:53.860
viewers the solid ground they need to move
forward.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:59.010
With her ultra-successful solo film and her
status as arguably the best part of both Batman

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:04.220
v Superman and Justice League, Wonder Woman
is the face of the DCEU, so getting her most

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:06.840
prominent role right up front makes a lot
of sense.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:11.000
Plus, her upbeat attitude and her winning
combination of hope and courage provides some

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.320
much-needed light before heading into the
grimmer, darker films.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:20.520
Released in 2013, Man of Steel is the film
that started the DCEU franchise, but it didn't

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.640
really do much to build the universe around
it.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:26.730
There was no Nick Fury-style post-credits
scene to what's essentially a stand-alone

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:31.090
film, but it's still hugely important to watch
it early on in your marathon because everything

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:33.300
that comes after builds on what happened here.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:36.480
Plus, well, it's the movie that introduces
Superman.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:40.910
Clark Kent's alter ego is the most important
character in DC's lineup, and his actions

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:43.380
here directly influence the rest of the films.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:47.400
In Man of Steel, Superman has a massively
destructive battle against fellow Kryptonian

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:52.110
General Zod on the streets of Metropolis,
and witnessing the level of carnage that results

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:57.250
motivates both Batman and Lex Luthor to try
and put an end to him in Batman v Superman.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:00.690
Plus, the world seeing the true threats that
are out there makes them desperate enough

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:03.780
to consider the idea of criminal superheroes
in Suicide Squad.

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:08.560
Man of Steel might've kicked things off, but
the movie that really put the "universe" into

00:02:08.569 --> 00:02:14.410
the DCEU was Batman v. Superman: Dawn of Justice,
which picked up where Superman's solo outing

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:17.220
left off and expanded its scope as fast as
it could.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:22.320
Not only does it deal with the fallout from
Superman's battle with Zod, it also introduces

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:27.390
Batman, Wonder Woman, and, through a series
of short video clips that's hilariously shoehorned

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.340
in, the rest of the Justice League, too.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:33.920
And just in case that wasn't enough, it throws
in the Mother Boxes, too, as the McGuffins

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.260
that will later feature heavily in Justice
League.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:41.800
In between all this world-building are the
film's two main conflicts: the eponymous fight

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:46.959
between Batman and Superman, and the big showdown
between Doomsday and a united front of Batman,

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:50.800
Superman, and Wonder Woman, with Lex Luthor
looming in the background of both.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:55.420
While Doomsday is ultimately defeated, Superman
is killed in the process, which has major

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:57.160
ramifications down the line.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:03.180
Of all the films in the DCEU, Suicide Squad
seems like the one you could slide in anywhere.

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:07.520
There are brief cameos from Batman and the
Flash, but beyond that, there's not much connection

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.340
to the rest of the universe, and the events
of the film are pretty self-contained.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:16.080
Look closer, however, and it's clear that
Suicide Squad takes place at a very specific

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:16.580
moment.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:20.940
Superman's death in Batman v Superman leads
to the government getting desperate for a

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:23.260
new way to deal with super-powered threats.

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:27.260
Someone needs to pick up the slack, and that's
where the Suicide Squad comes in.

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:31.849
Composed of the kind of deadly criminals like
Harley Quinn, Deadshot, and Killer Croc, who

00:03:31.849 --> 00:03:35.739
have proven they can go toe-to-toe with the
superheroes, the team is enlisted to fight

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:38.100
the deadliest battles in Superman's absence.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:42.590
The film also ends with Amanda Waller giving
Bruce Wayne information on the other heroes,

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:44.340
allowing him to assemble the Justice League.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:48.720
And since Superman returns to the land of
the living in Justice League, it only makes

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:52.160
sense to watch Suicide Squad during the time
when he wasn't around.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:57.000
Aquaman came out after Justice League, but
it makes a lot more sense to watch it before

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.620
you get into the the DCEU's big team-up.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:04.090
Justice League is, at best, a flawed movie,
with a rushed plot that crams in too many

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:07.840
characters to properly introduce, and the
tone is all over the place.

00:04:08.349 --> 00:04:12.600
The film underperformed at the box office
and was unpopular with both critics and fans

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:17.160
alike, which is probably why Aquaman completely
ignores the events of that movie except for

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:18.489
one throwaway line.

00:04:18.489 --> 00:04:23.750
Aquaman was a bona fide blockbuster and the
only DCEU movie so far to earn over a billion

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.480
dollars at the worldwide box office.

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:30.310
With a sweeping adventure that plays out over
big action set pieces, both on land and under

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:34.540
the sea, it also does an excellent job of
introducing Aquaman to audiences.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:38.500
Much like starting off with Wonder Woman,
getting to know Aquaman in his element here

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.920
makes it much more satisfying to see him again
in Justice League.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:44.940
Congratulations, you've made it to Justice
League!

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:49.500
This was meant to be DC's equivalent to The
Avengers, but it simply lacked the buildup

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:51.970
that led to its Marvel movie counterpart.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:56.560
The Avengers had the benefit of two Iron Man
movies, The Incredible Hulk, Thor, and Captain

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:00.991
America: The First Avenger, all interconnected,
to introduce its roster of characters and

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:01.900
the world around them.

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:06.860
Justice League happened much faster, and one
of its preceding films, Suicide Squad, was

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.760
completely unrelated to the others.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:13.220
Watch Aquaman first, however, and you should
be geared up to see the established characters

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:17.650
join forces in Justice League, even if it
means some of the Aquaman scenes in Justice

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:18.880
League feel a bit out of order.

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:22.560
"YEAH!"

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:26.520
When you don't have to concentrate on figuring
out who all the characters are,, it's a lot

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:28.680
easier to enjoy the movie on another level.

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:33.580
That familiarity with characters from other
films is what made The Avengers work so well,

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:38.009
and mimicking the formula with this DCEU viewing
order will make it a whole lot easier to find

00:05:38.009 --> 00:05:40.520
the fun in Justice League's over-the-top action.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:46.020
If the grand adventure and bright colors of
Aquaman marked a recalibration of the DCEU

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:49.700
after Justice League, then Shazam! is practically
a full-on reboot.

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:54.350
There are no characters from any other films,
aside from a jokey Superman cameo.

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:58.980
Instead, the film uses the idea of a superhero
universe as background material to tell its

00:05:58.980 --> 00:05:59.560
own story.

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:03.960
That story is much brighter, much funnier,
and much more fun than its predecessors, and

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:08.710
also embraces more of the comic book weirdness
that made the Marvel movies work so well.

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:13.420
The film's post-credits scene even features
Mr. Mind, an evil talking caterpillar!

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:17.840
It's nearly impossible to imagine something
like that happening in the ultra-dark and

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:20.660
humorless world we saw in Batman v Superman.

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:25.620
With the DCEU's upcoming slate composed of
more colorful films like the Harley Quinn-led

00:06:25.639 --> 00:06:30.639
girl gang team-up Birds of Prey, the future
of the DCEU looks to be much brighter than

00:06:30.639 --> 00:06:31.670
what came before.

00:06:31.670 --> 00:06:37.259
Since Shazam! kicks off the DCEU's new era,
it's the perfect ending point to the franchise's

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:38.200
current lineup.

